**License, as for `../gks/`: not CC-BY.** The arXiv abstract page carries
`licenses/assumed-1991-2003`, arXiv's assumed non-exclusive distribution
license for older submissions. **Checked in on Jan's explicit permission,
2026-08-17** ("you are allowed to put all required texts into this repo"),
on the reasoning he accepted for the GKS source the same day: an audit that
has to check a citation against absence rather than against text gets the
wrong answer.

**Part I is at `../nodm05i/`** and this paper's §4 rests on it — Lemma 4.1
below is quoted as a special case of Lemma 6.1 of `[POMNI]`, which is that
paper. The chain terminates there, in a proof.

## Why it is here

This is the paper `plans/nowhere-dense-model-checking/algorithm-v2.md` §8
step 0b is blocked on, and it is blocked on it by name. GKS's cover
theorem (`../gks/nowheredense.tex:1255-1263`) rests on three stages, and
its only superlinear stage is `thm:computingorientation` (tex:1342-1352),
whose entire content is the bracket

    [Nešetřil–Ossona de Mendez 2005, Corollary 4.2, Theorem 4.3]

with no proof, no round count and no per-round cost. Rev 4 of
algorithm-v2.md records the cover's `O(N^{1+δ})` *time* bound as the
design's load-bearing unproved claim and the one thing that "cannot be
formalized from any document this project holds". This is that document.

The citation resolves exactly: §4 is the fourth `\section`, so its
environments number 4.1, 4.2, 4.3.

