                             and md(G_i) along the augmentation chain
        570    §4.2 the one-step algorithm, in pseudocode:
                 transitivity arcs   O(md(G)²·n), ≤ md(G)²·n added
                 fraternity edges    O(md(G)²·n), |L| ≤ md(G)²·n/2
                 simplify L, orient it at low indegree, merge  O(md(G)²·n)
                 and the indegree recurrence md(G_{i+1}) ≤ md(G_i)² + 2∇_0(G_i),
                 i.e. F(x,y) = x² + 2y  (stated at :570-571)
        679    Theorem 4.3 — for a class of BOUNDED EXPANSION and fixed c,
                             computes G_1 ⊆ … ⊆ G_c in time O(n)
   690  Distances — O(1) capped-distance queries after linear preprocessing
   716  p-centered colorings and tree-decomposition
